# autoload/spacemacs_theme.vim is the Vim 8.x compatibility shim: it contains
# no `def` at all, only legacy `function! spacemacs_theme#set()`, and a legacy
# autoload function may only be defined in a file whose name matches its
# prefix.  This harness sources a *copy* under a tempname, so that file — and
# only that file — reports E746 for reasons that have nothing to do with its
# contents.  There is also nothing for :defcompile to do in it.
#
# The previous entry was the glob `spacemacs_theme*.vim`, whose stated reason
# was that ":defcompile rejects them on principle rather than because anything
# is wrong".  That was false for autoload/spacemacs_theme_v9.vim: the glob was
# hiding a real E1267 that made :SpacemacsThemeToggle, :SpacemacsThemeDark and
# :SpacemacsThemeLight dead on every supported Vim.  Do not widen it again.
spacemacs_theme.vim
